WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.899
hi it's Michelle from Lab Muffin
beauty science and today we're going to

00:00:03.899 --> 00:00:08.910
be talking about hair more specifically
I'm going to be talking about what

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:14.400
olaplex is and how it works
olaplex is a brand that's been huge in

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:19.439
the hair world since it came onto the
market in 2014 it's the reason why my

00:00:19.439 --> 00:00:23.369
hair is currently this dusty purple
color and still attached to my hair

00:00:23.369 --> 00:00:28.529
after a single 8 and 1/2 hour marathon
hair session it's pretty much

00:00:28.529 --> 00:00:33.630
revolutionised hair bleaching and it's
spawned a billion imitations there's

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:37.110
actually a lawsuit going on right now
over whether or not there's been an

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:42.780
infringement of olaplex's patent now
I'm not an employee of olaplex I'm not

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:46.739
being paid by olaplex I've never met
them I have nothing to do with them I'm

00:00:46.739 --> 00:00:50.809
just a cosmetic science nerd and there's
a lot of cool science behind the product

00:00:50.809 --> 00:00:57.620
let's get started

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:02.489
olaplex is a brand of hair products that
contains a special active ingredient

00:01:02.489 --> 00:01:07.260
that can join up the broken bonds in
hair it can be added to hair coloring

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:12.920
products to minimize damage or it can be
used as a separate repairing treatment

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:18.090
the active ingredient in these olaplex
products is called bisaminopropyl

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:22.330
diglycol dimaleate and it looks like
this

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:26.920
this little guy is the reason why olaplex
works to restore hair that's been

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:31.780
damaged from too much bleaching too much
heat styling or just being beaten up

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:36.220
over time but to understand how it works
we're going to have to have a closer

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:45.970
look at the structure of hair and what
happens when you bleach it if you've

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:49.660
ever looked at hair products you'll know
that the word protein is thrown around a

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:55.120
lot which makes sense because hair is
mostly made of protein it's mostly a

00:01:55.120 --> 00:02:00.400
protein called keratin which you've
probably heard of before nails are made

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:05.410
of the same keratin as hair proteins
are really long chains of amino acids

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:10.030
and keratin contains a whole bunch of an
amino acid called cysteine which is

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:15.580
special because it contains sulfur atoms
which has the symbol s these sulfur

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:19.959
atoms can make two bonds and when
they're oxidized like from being exposed

00:02:19.959 --> 00:02:25.120
to oxygen in the air they'll form bonds
with each other like this it's like

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:28.900
they're holding hands
these are called disulfide bonds because

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:34.780
they have two sulfurs sometimes they
also called cystine inside the hair all

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:39.070
of these microscopic little disulfide
bonds join the hair together like glue

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:44.019
so you end up with really strong hair
this glue also sticks hair together and

00:02:44.019 --> 00:02:47.940
gives it its shape whether it's curly or
straight

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:56.890
the reason that natural hair is colored
is the melanin pigment which has a

00:02:56.890 --> 00:03:00.420
structure which looks a bit like this

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:06.150
in chemistry this is called a conjugated
system with alternating double and

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:10.650
single bonds and this means that it's
really good at absorbing light black

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:15.510
hair for example absorbs all of the
colors of light but if you break this

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:19.890
conjugation the melanin pigment can't
absorb light anymore so it ends up

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:25.530
looking white within hair bleach there's
an alkali like ammonia and hydrogen

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:30.329
peroxide to break up the melanin but it
takes a bit of time for the bleaching to

00:03:30.329 --> 00:03:34.769
work and because the bleach mixture is
super reactive it can react with other

00:03:34.769 --> 00:03:39.290
bits of your hair in the meantime such
as your strong keratin proteins in

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:44.069
practice after about half of the
disulfide bonds in your hair can be

00:03:44.069 --> 00:03:50.310
broken during a severe bleaching session
normally if you expose your hair to

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:55.020
oxygen the sulfur-sulfur bonds will
eventually form again but just to really

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:59.670
mess with your hair hydrogen peroxide can
actually cap off the sulfur so it can't

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:04.530
form these disulfide bonds again to mess
up your hair even more peroxide can also

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:08.970
react with other amino acids and it can
also break up the peptide bonds that are

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:13.770
joining each of the amino acids together
in your hair and so eventually you end

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:24.180
up with weak brittle damaged hair the
ingredient in olaplex which is

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:29.160
bisaminopropyl diglycol dimaleate can
actually join the sulfur atoms in your

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:33.540
hair back together again it reacts with
the sulfur atoms through a reaction

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:39.000
called a Michael addition and it acts as
a link between the two sulfurs the two

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:43.530
maleate ends of the olaplex complex
joined to a sulfur atom each and the

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:49.140
bisaminopropyl diglycol part joins it
all together so you end up with joined

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:53.940
up sulfur atoms the really nifty thing
is that this reaction between the

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:58.200
olaplex ingredient and your hair happens
much faster than the reaction where

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:03.060
hydrogen peroxide caps off the sulfur
and stops it from reacting so when the

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:07.170
olaplex is mixed in with the hair bleach
and applied to hair it actually forms

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:11.580
these bridges and stops the capping
reaction from happening so the damage

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:15.990
during bleaching that's usually
irreversible isn't irreversible anymore

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:20.940
which is pretty cool it's so good at
preventing damage that my course black

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:25.860
Asian hair could be dyed to white in one
long sitting without it all breaking off

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:30.660
I can still hear style it I can gently
comb it while it's wet and it doesn't

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:35.430
break off when I brush it before olaplex
came along I wouldn't have been able to

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:40.200
get my hair to this color while leaving
it in a reasonable condition to make the

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:44.340
bleached hair even stronger there are a
few more steps of olaplex still with

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:49.230
the same active ingredient and the same
mechanism of action after bleaching with

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:53.730
step one there's step two which is applied
to your hair for 10 to 20 minutes after

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:58.650
the bleach is washed out this joins up
more of the cysteine sulfur atoms after

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:02.849
that there step 3 which is a take-home
treatment with a lower concentration of

00:06:02.849 --> 00:06:07.879
olaplex which is applied for about 10 to
20 minutes again and then rinsed out

00:06:07.879 --> 00:06:12.629
there's also a new shampoo and
conditioner imaginatively named 4 &amp; 5

00:06:12.629 --> 00:06:18.590
that also contain the same active
ingredient and they work the same way

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:27.120
it isn't just bleaching that you can use
olaplex for it will work whenever broken

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:32.340
disulfide bonds are an issue which is a
lot of things pretty much all types of

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:37.050
hair damage will break sulfur-sulfur
bonds for example if you use high pH

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:42.180
alkaline products like hair dye or high
pH shampoos if you have thermal damage

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:45.810
from using too much heat on your hair
like hair curlers and hair straighteners

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:50.370
and blow dryers if your hair gets
exposed to visible and UV light from the

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:54.810
Sun when you brush and style your hair
especially when it's wet and fragile you

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:58.650
can end up with lots of mechanical
damage this also happens if you

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:02.310
vigorously rub your hair dry with a
towel if you use other chemical

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:06.599
treatments on your hair like perming and
straightening in all of these cases an

00:07:06.599 --> 00:07:11.339
olaplex hair treatment can help repair
the damage it will soften and strengthen

00:07:11.339 --> 00:07:15.509
damaged hair and it can restore the
texture of natural curls you can even

00:07:15.509 --> 00:07:20.759
use it to tame beards the bonds that the
olaplex forms in the hair are claimed to

00:07:20.759 --> 00:07:25.139
be permanent and supposedly it won't
wash out but like the original disulfide

00:07:25.139 --> 00:07:29.279
bonds they can still break so over time
your hair can still deteriorate in

00:07:29.279 --> 00:07:34.349
condition and that's all for today if
you want to find out more you can look

00:07:34.349 --> 00:07:37.379
at the olaplex blog post that i've
linked in the caption which has a bit

00:07:37.379 --> 00:07:41.339
more detail about all of this if you
enjoyed this video I would really

00:07:41.339 --> 00:07:44.849
appreciate it if you liked it and
subscribed to my channel you can also

00:07:44.849 --> 00:07:48.779
find out more about the science behind
other beauty products in my blog and you

00:07:48.779 --> 00:07:53.789
